{
  "id": "COMPOUND:16860 - PROTEIN:6323",
  "verbalization": "Licochalcone G is implicated in the regulation of DNA polymerase iota through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Licochalcone G acts as a target for multiple compounds, including phosphodiesterase 6C, which in turn targets DNA polymerase iota. This indicates a potential regulatory pathway where Licochalcone G may influence the activity of phosphodiesterase 6C, which then modulates DNA polymerase iota. The presence of multiple targets for phosphodiesterase 6C, such as (2S,3R,4S)-2-[(14S)-14-hydroxypentadecyl]-4-methyl-5-oxooxolane-3-carboxylic acid and Talathermophilins B, further supports the idea that Licochalcone G may exert its effects through a network of molecular intermediates that ultimately lead to the regulation of DNA polymerase iota. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship, with Licochalcone G potentially playing a role in the activation or inhibition of DNA polymerase iota through the modulation of its upstream targets.",
